<title>SINGAPORE: TABLE-OUB 1st-half net profit up 27.2 pct.</title>
<headline>TABLE-OUB 1st-half net profit up 27.2 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1997</p>
<p>		   (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			    180.85 vs  142.15</p>
<p>Dividend (cents)			5.00 vs    5.00</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)		    26.59 vs   20.91</p>
<p>    Group interest income	    1196.61 vs  905.26</p>
<p>    Group interest expense	    813.95 vs  583.13</p>
<p>    Group net interest income	 382.65 vs  322.12</p>
<p>    Group dividends			 7.56 vs    6.57</p>
<p>    Group fees and commissions	 84.17 vs   75.87</p>
<p>    Group other income		   25.25 vs   17.34</p>
<p>    Group operating expenses	  245.30 vs  223.97</p>
<p>    Group pretax profit		 254.33 vs  197.94</p>
<p>    Group tax				68.45 vs   52.43</p>
<p>    Group minorities			5.03 vs    3.36</p>
<p>    Bank shr (cents)		     18.94 vs   15.24</p>
<p>Dividend pay: September 12, 1997</p>
<p>Last day books open: September 1, 1997</p>
<p>Note - Full name Overseas Union Bank Ltd (OUB).</p>
